       'Map the range onto the customer decision tree of the category (the order in which shoppers choose: need or use, type, brand, size, price tier) and count the options per branch and per good-better-best tier; duplication is two lines answering the same need at the same price point, a gap is a branch or tier with demand and no option.',
       'Test each delist candidate for its role before cutting it: entry price point, range credibility, exclusive or own-label line, basket builder bought with high-margin lines, supplier terms that depend on it.',
       'Estimate transferable demand for each delist: the share of its sales likely to move to the closest remaining substitute (high where a near duplicate stays, low where the line is unique), stated as an assumption with a range.',
